  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ab9abe63-2771-5116-81b8-eac1cddd0e28" activityNameId="a85e4d03-a39a-5f89-9cf6-1072061aaf5d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Heavy fuel oil, burned in refinery furnace</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Heavy fuel oil, burned in refinery furnace
Description of the direct emissions due to the combustion of heavy fuel oil in refinery furnaces and generators not including the infrastructure of the furnace.;
Synonyms: Schweröl, HFO; 
UUID: b32a475e-1842-3f7b-a6d0-5522bc48d5a9
Consumption of heavy fuel oil and combustion emissions.
Location: Data for Swiss and single European plants.
Technology: Average technology in use.
Time period: New Swiss data for regulated emissions CO2, NOx, SOx, Ni and V have been provided by the refineries. They have been compared and discussed with older literature data. European data have been used for other emissions.
Production volume: 47 thousand tonnes of heavy fuel oil were burned in 2000.
Sampling: Literature survey and plant data. 
Extrapolations: Some emissions are estimated with European figures.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b32a475e-1842-3f7b-a6d0-5522bc48d5a9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
